{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/BufferingResource","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BufferingResource"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Expensive interaction with the underlying resource is minimized, since most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(smaller) requests can be satisfied by accessing the buffer alone. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawback is that some extra space is required to hold the buffer and that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copying takes place when filling that buffer, but this is usually","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outweighed by the performance benefits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that this implementation is pretty limited and the benefits are only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apparent when reading forward and consecutively – e.g. when downloading the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resource by chunks. The buffer is ignored when reading backward or far","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ahead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Wraps an existing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Resource","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and buffers its content.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/BufferingResource\/init(resource:bufferSize:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc